<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="023" project="email-communication-intelligence-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Indexed sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash column + backfill decision</title>
    <phase>2 Pillar C — De-duplication</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New Dataverse schema surface (one indexed column) via dataverse-create-schema + a recorded backfill decision; no .cs/.ts code change. STANDARD per task-create Step 3.5.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single schema artifact (one indexed string column) with a known recipe. The only judgment is the backfill decision, which is bounded and documented, not architectural.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>schema-c</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Schema-only on `sprk_document`, disjoint from task 020's key on `sprk_communication`. No shared source files with any active worktree.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, schema, dedup</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1.5-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create a new INDEXED `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash` column to hold the SPE content identity (`quickXorHash` from `driveItem.file.hashes` — `sha256Hash` is DEPRECATED on SPE), packed into the managed solution (ADR-027). Record the backfill decision for already-persisted documents (model on `scripts/Backfill-DocumentHasFile.ps1`). This column is the storage the task-024 content-dedup detector queries.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Dataverse schema expertise. Use `dataverse-create-schema` (Web API + PowerShell — no `pac column create`). Follow ADR-027 strictly.</role>
  <goal>An indexed string column `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash` exists, published, and carried in the managed solution; a recorded backfill decision (backfill now vs lazy-on-next-touch vs defer) with rationale + a modeled script path lives in notes/. Verified in `spaarkedev1`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-C3 absorbs `sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1`. The detector (task 024) needs an indexed column on `sprk_document` holding the content hash so byte-identical uploads are found before a second canonical document is created. The chosen identity is `quickXorHash` (from `driveItem.file.hashes`); `sha256Hash` is deprecated on SPE. The `sprk_document` models live in `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs`. This task creates ONLY the column + records the backfill decision; task 024 wires the detector. Backfill is **forward-only** — no historical reprocessing of already-persisted documents (owner decision 2026-08-05). There is **no spike gate**: task 024's gate-after-write approach fixes the identity as `quickXorHash` (read from `driveItem.file.hashes` after upload completes), so the column semantics are settled and this task is startable now.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs (sprk_document model — column mapping, added by task 024)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Backfill-DocumentHasFile.ps1 (model the backfill script shape on this)</file>
      <file role="modify">Dataverse managed solution — sprk_document entity metadata</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <!-- Task 001 (SPE spike 1) removed: gate-after-write (task 024, owner decision 2026-08-05) settles the identity as quickXorHash read post-upload; no spike gate. This task is startable with no dependencies. -->
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: identity + backfill + gating (owner decision 2026-08-05). The column's identity is `quickXorHash` (read from `driveItem.file.hashes` AFTER upload completes per task 024's gate-after-write). Backfill is **forward-only** — no historical reprocessing of already-persisted documents. There is **no spike gate**; this task is startable now (spike 1 retired).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">SCOPE: the new column. Author into the managed solution + export so it deploys to every subscription; do NOT create it unmanaged in one environment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: indexing. The column MUST be indexed (queryable for equality-hit lookup at scale by task 024); a non-indexed column degrades detector performance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: identity source. The column holds `quickXorHash` from `driveItem.file.hashes` — `sha256Hash` is DEPRECATED on SPE and MUST NOT be used as the identity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: backfill. Record an explicit backfill decision (backfill-now / lazy / defer) with a concrete rationale and a modeled script path (`scripts/Backfill-DocumentHasFile.ps1` shape); do NOT run a mass backfill without recording the decision + escalating if it mutates many production rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: schema mechanism. Use `dataverse-create-schema` (Web API + PowerShell); PAC CLI has no column-create path here.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse indexed column for SPE content-hash de-duplication + backfill strategy</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-027-subscription-isolation-and-dataverse-solution-management.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/agent-memory/researcher/spe-dedup-content-identity-2026-07.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/communication-service-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="dataverse-create-schema" location=".claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md">Create the indexed string column via Web API; enable the index; pack to solution.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Backfill script model" location="scripts/Backfill-DocumentHasFile.ps1">Shape for a paged, resumable, non-fatal backfill if the decision is backfill-now.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load POML + project CLAUDE.md + spec FR-C3/NFR-08 + ADR-027/007 + the researcher SPE-dedup memo. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: STANDARD. Identity = quickXorHash, backfill forward-only, no spike gate (owner 2026-08-05). Invoke dataverse-create-schema.</step>
    <step order="1">Create the indexed string column `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash` (length sufficient for a quickXorHash value) via the skill; enable the index; poll to Active.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the entity + column to the managed solution; export; verify the column is in the export.</step>
    <step order="3">Decide + record the backfill strategy in notes/ (backfill-now vs lazy vs defer), with rationale and a modeled `scripts/Backfill-Document*Hash*.ps1` path. Do NOT execute a mass backfill without escalation.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify in `spaarkedev1`: the column exists, is indexed, and accepts a sample quickXorHash value.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviation (incl. spike-1-driven semantics changes) in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a quickXorHash value cannot fit the created column length or the column cannot be indexed for equality lookup at scale (e.g. the platform rejects the index on the chosen length), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 before shipping a column that silently truncates the hash or cannot serve the detector's equality lookup.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No hash/content-identity column on `sprk_document` (grep of `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs` shows document-type + SPE-pointer fields but no canonical-hash). `sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1` designed this but shipped no code/schema.</existing>
    <extension>No — the existing SPE-pointer fields (driveId/itemId) identify the STORAGE location, not the CONTENT; two byte-identical uploads have different pointers. A content-hash column is a distinct, indexed identity with no existing field to reuse.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without an indexed content-hash column, byte-identical files duplicate silently in SPE across every upload path (incl. email attachments) with no cross-container dedup authority — FR-C3's core failure. The detector (task 024) has nowhere to look up a hit.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dataverse-create-schema">Create the indexed column via Web API + PowerShell</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Solution export + backfill-script modeling</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="schema">Indexed sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash column</output>
    <output type="solution">Managed solution export containing the column</output>
    <output type="notes">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/ — backfill decision + rationale + modeled script path</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the deployed schema, when the attribute is queried, then `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash` exists, is a string, and is indexed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the managed solution export, when inspected, then the column definition is present (deploys to every subscription per ADR-027).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a sample quickXorHash value, when written to the column in `spaarkedev1`, then it persists and is queryable by equality.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A backfill decision (backfill-now / lazy / defer) with rationale + a modeled script path is recorded in notes/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the column length is sufficient for a full quickXorHash value so a written hash is NOT silently truncated (a round-tripped sample hash equals the value written); if the chosen length/index cannot hold or index the hash, the task escalated rather than shipping a truncating column.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-C3; plan Phase 2 C3 (schema half). Pairs with task 020 in parallel-group schema-c. Feeds task 024 (detector). Identity = quickXorHash (sha256Hash deprecated). Backfill forward-only (owner 2026-08-05). Tier-2 (near-dup / documentVector3072) is deferred OUT of R2 (owner 2026-08-05) — NOT this task.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
